                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "25279370-06d2-4065-ba00-6dc709bbb208",
                        "source_entry_id": "04c0ca11-1512-34b5-8c16-7854b1ba3293",
                        "source_sense_id": "3b10ea72-5af2-3bce-815d-e145d25eab59",
                        "target_lang_word": "iguana",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "iguana",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eda67d8a-f426-3cef-8408-532a730da5f1",
                                        "entry_id": "a08944d3-0ca7-37ce-bcd6-610272db6157",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A green iguana (Iguana iguana), a large tropical American lizard often kept as a pet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7afd4f28-e74d-4391-b428-10b04f588267",
                                                "sense_id": "eda67d8a-f426-3cef-8408-532a730da5f1",
                                                "text": "The problem with keeping the green iguana as a pet is that they are often misfed. For example, some will feed them meat or meat-based foods […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6da25fec-be95-3ea8-8443-03a9c0ca4500",
                                        "entry_id": "a08944d3-0ca7-37ce-bcd6-610272db6157",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any member of the genus Iguana."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "689578fe-ccf1-30e2-b44c-95d1ba837b9d",
                                        "entry_id": "a08944d3-0ca7-37ce-bcd6-610272db6157",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In America and the Pacific, any of several members of the lizard family Iguanidae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4826fa71-7ef2-43a2-bcba-913ee7ace551",
                                                "sense_id": "689578fe-ccf1-30e2-b44c-95d1ba837b9d",
                                                "text": "Marine iguanas line the shores of the islands, and are usually seen sprawled over lava rocks near the sea."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca3e2891-5346-34b6-a99e-3178c0ec9161",
                                        "entry_id": "a08944d3-0ca7-37ce-bcd6-610272db6157",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In Africa, any large member of the genus Varanus, especially the aquatic Nile monitor (see leguan)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75fd7eb3-fba2-35ec-ab03-81d12c5e47a8",
                                        "entry_id": "a08944d3-0ca7-37ce-bcd6-610272db6157",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any member of the genus Varanus (see goanna)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe565b07-1185-45b6-b22a-6d468a1f67e4",
                                                "sense_id": "75fd7eb3-fba2-35ec-ab03-81d12c5e47a8",
                                                "text": "The last they had had, was an iguana one of the blacks had brought in; and though he felt disgusted at the idea of eating it, he made up into a kind of stew, and they both enjoyed it immensely."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "874cb055-955b-4aa6-be73-91ae1d70737d",
                        "source_entry_id": "04c0ca11-1512-34b5-8c16-7854b1ba3293",
                        "source_sense_id": "3b10ea72-5af2-3bce-815d-e145d25eab59",
                        "target_lang_word": "iguana",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "iguana",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a799ce2a-286f-33a7-b5ca-9c2536ae0f0d",
                                        "entry_id": "177079e6-1677-3761-8a30-70ea2d25f48c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(Iguana spp.) Cualquiera de dos especies de lagartos nativos de las regiones tropicales de América y el Caribe, caracterizadas por una cresta dorsal, la presencia de grandes escamas tuberculares en el cuello y una longitud que alcanza los dos metros."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "epicene"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95106124-8d43-4cd9-8fe1-782626536eaa",
                                                "sense_id": "a799ce2a-286f-33a7-b5ca-9c2536ae0f0d",
                                                "text": "Hecha nuestra montería, seguimos el camino adelante, y a poco rato hallé algunos de los corredores que iban delante parados, y tenían cuatro indios cazadores que había tomado, y traían muerto un león y ciertas iguanas, que son unos grandes lagartos que hay en las islas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "608cddfb-b187-4850-8448-46193a5bbf18",
                                                "sense_id": "a799ce2a-286f-33a7-b5ca-9c2536ae0f0d",
                                                "text": "La iguana también la comen en los campos. Es un animal limpio que se alimenta de limpias hierbas. En la rama donde está la agitan hasta que cae atontada; entonces la cazan y la llevan a la cocinera. Yo he comido iguana y confieso que se asemeja a la carne de gallina y que no siendo de muy fino paladar pueden confundirse."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d8f64886-5496-4a67-a1f5-8a18c9bc245c",
                        "source_entry_id": "04c0ca11-1512-34b5-8c16-7854b1ba3293",
                        "source_sense_id": "3b10ea72-5af2-3bce-815d-e145d25eab59",
